| Best for | Reminders and same-chat follow-ups | Repeated or one-shot standalone coding work |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"If a task depends on unstated chat history, needs an interactive approval halfway through, or should"},{"id":"p16s2","text":" react to a file, HTTP, or process condition rather than time, it is not a good automation yet."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## ✨ Features"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### 🕹️ One control plane, two ways in"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- **DSH Web:** open **Automations** from the sidebar or the conversation tab to create a rule, pause"},{"id":"p19s2","text":" or resume it, run it now, delete it, and inspect recent runs. On the blank New Session screen, the "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"sidebar shortcut tells you to start a conversation instead of failing silently.
- **Any eligible roo"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"t Agent:** ask in natural language. Six scoped tools let the Agent manage automations only for its e"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"in natural language. Six scoped tools let the Agent manage automations only for its exact workspace."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"There is no separate bot, daemon UI, or third-party scheduler to operate."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### 📅 Schedules people can read"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Create a one-shot, fixed-interval, daily, or weekly rule. Daily and weekly schedules use an IANA tim"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"e zone; the friendly form is normalized into a validated RFC 5545 RRULE for persistence and inspecti"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"one; the friendly form is normalized into a validated RFC 5545 RRULE for persistence and inspection."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### 🧠 A model target for each automation"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"The Web form can follow the live global model or pin one provider/model pair. A pinned model can use"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" its own default reasoning effort or one of the opaque effort values advertised by that exact model."},{"id":"p24s3","text":" The card shows the saved target, and each run keeps the same target in its immutable snapshot."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Agent tools expose the same fields. Omitting all model fields on create preserves the existing behav"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"ior of capturing the creating Session's complete selection; explicitly setting `provider` and `model"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"` to `null` follows the live global selection at run time. On update, omitted fields stay unchanged,"},{"id":"p25s4","text":" `null` clears a pin, and changing the route without an effort resets to the new model's default."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"### 🧼 A clean execution boundary every time"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Each dispatched occurrence receives:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- a new Session ID and fresh root Agent;
- the saved prompt, not the source conversation history;
- "},{"id":"p28s2","text":"the captured workspace, cwd, Agent preset, permission preset, and a durable model target that either"},{"id":"p28s3","text":" follows the live global selection or pins one model and optional reasoning effort;
- an explicit `a"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"utomation` message source containing the automation ID, run ID, and scheduled time;
- a terminal res"},{"id":"p28s5","text":"ult derived from the actual DSH turn end, not merely “message delivered.”"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"### 🧾 History that explains failure as well as success"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Runs progress through `queued`, `running`, and a terminal state such as `succeeded`, `failed`, `skip"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"ped`, or `cancelled`. Each record keeps its definition revision, prompt and target snapshot, schedul"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"ed time, result Session ID, bounded summary, and structured error."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Updating a definition increments its revision, so each retained run still identifies what it execute"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"d. Deleting the definition does not immediately erase those run records. Retention removes only the "},{"id":"p31s3","text":"oldest terminal records; queued and running records are never pruned."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Set `archiveRunSessions: true` in the Cordis plugin config to archive completed, failed, cancelled, "},{"id":"p32s2","text":"and other terminal run Sessions from the ordinary DSH conversation list. Their logs are not deleted:"},{"id":"p32s3","text":" the Automations run history keeps the Session ID, summary, and error as an auditable inbox. Current"},{"id":"p32s4","text":" Harness releases do not expose an unarchive API, so an archived result is labeled instead of offeri"},{"id":"p32s5","text":"ng a broken Session-open action. The default is `false` and preserves ordinary Session navigation."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## ⚡ Install"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Install the GitHub bundle into the DSH Web profile, then restart `dsh web`:"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"The version tag keeps the install reproducible; a reviewed commit SHA is equally valid. If you run D"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"SH from its source checkout, use `pnpm dsh` in place of `dsh`."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"Install from a local checkout"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Node.js 22.19 or newer is required."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"The repository ships its built Host and Web bundles. Git installation runs no
package build script a"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"nd needs no `allowBuilds` entry."},{"id":"p41s1","text":"## 🚀 Quick start"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"### 🖥️ From DSH Web"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"1. Open a Session attached to the workspace you want to automate.
2. Open **Automations** from the s"},{"id":"p43s2","text":"idebar, or select it next to Chat and Trajectory. If the New Session screen is still blank, start th"},{"id":"p43s3","text":"e conversation first.
